{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorAssembly","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorAssembly","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorTargetSpec","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.MarkovWeightValueTransport"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorAssembly.assembled_equal_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorAssembly.assembled_equal_split","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauFunctorAssembly.lean#L114-L120","doc":"The equal-split consequence at the derived weight, end to end: the\nconjugate block of the assembled operator also carries `5/2` — the ½ of\n`½·a₀` instantiated at the parameter-free target (via the spec's\n`discharge_equal_split`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorAssembly.assembled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorAssembly.assembled","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauFunctorAssembly.lean#L88-L112","doc":"**Packaging (labeled, per the spec's honesty rule): the parameter-free\ntarget.** The T1-structured operator inhabits `ArchimedeanTauRealization` at\nthe DERIVED weight `w = 5/2`. Inhabitation itself is trivial (the spec proves\nso); the content is that no free parameter remains — T5's obligation is now\nprovenance for THIS target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorAssembly.canonicalLoopWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorAssembly.canonicalLoopWeight","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauFunctorAssembly.lean#L81-L86","doc":"The assembled loop-weight operator on `H^{1,0} ⊕ H^{0,1}`: the weight\nblock on each factor, conjugate blocks equal (the shape T3's deck-reality\nequivariance forces), off-diagonal blocks zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorAssembly.weightBlock_conjTranspose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorAssembly.weightBlock_conjTranspose","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauFunctorAssembly.lean#L74-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorAssembly.weightBlock_map_star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorAssembly.weightBlock_map_star","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauFunctorAssembly.lean#L68-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorAssembly.weightBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorAssembly.weightBlock","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauFunctorAssembly.lean#L63-L66","doc":"The per-factor block: the weight profile as a (real-entried) diagonal\noperator on one Hodge factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorAssembly.channelWeight_derived","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorAssembly.channelWeight_derived","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauFunctorAssembly.lean#L54-L61","doc":"**The derived channel weight**: `Σ_j weightProfile j = 5/2` — and this is\nexactly the T1-dims × T4-values pairing `3·y₂(1) + 1·y₁₁(1)`, a theorem of\nthe merged modules, not a chosen parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorAssembly.weightProfile","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorAssembly.weightProfile","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauFunctorAssembly.lean#L50-L52","doc":"The canonical channel-weight profile on H¹(Bring): the T4 value ¾ on the\nT1 moving block (dims 3), ¼ on the invariant line (dim 1). ","signatureChunk":0}]}